    "Title": "",
    "Text": "\"The Swiss Army knife of campus buildings 🔋📚☕\"\n\nThe Clough Undergraduate Learning Commons—aka CULC—isn’t just a building. It’s the campus hotspot where studying, socializing, and caffeine addiction unite in perfect harmony.\n\nWhat makes it awesome:\n\nOpen 24/7 – You can roll in at 3 a.m. to finish your lab report, cry into your notes, or discover your group project team actually can be productive.\n\nPerfect study vibes – From group pods to quiet corners, there’s a spot for every flavor of academic panic.\n\nThe Starbucks downstairs – Because nothing says “academic excellence” like a triple espresso at midnight.\n\nTech everywhere – Charging outlets for days, huge whiteboards, presentation rooms…basically productivity paradise.\n\nLocation – Smack in the middle of campus, so you can “accidentally” bump into friends between classes.\n\nEvery time I walk into CULC, I feel like I’m entering the mothership of Georgia Tech—bright, buzzing, and brimming with brilliant people. Whether you’re grinding out code, chatting over coffee, or just people-watching, this place fuels the Yellow Jacket hive mind.\n\nPro tip: The top floor is underrated—great sunlight, fewer people, and a chance to feel like you’re studying in a glass cloud.",
